Low Block - Feature Summary
Summary of features completed for the Low Block puzzle game (block-placement game on a 6x6 grid, similar to Block Blast).
🎮 Gameplay Features

Block rotation: clicking the ⟳ button rotates the currently selected tray block 90° clockwise
Fixed placement anchor bug: previously, clicking a cell that visually looked like the "top-left corner" of a shape could place it in the wrong position, because the anchor was based on the first element in the shape array rather than its actual top-left coordinate — fixed to always anchor correctly based on geometry
High score persistence (localStorage): best score is saved permanently across sessions, displayed with a 🏆 icon
Game state persistence (localStorage): the board, current score, and tray blocks are continuously saved — refreshing the page (F5) no longer resets progress. State is cleared automatically on game over or reset

🎨 UI & Effects

Thicker grid border (4px) + drop shadow (box-shadow) for a raised, tactile look
Rotate button perfectly centered using flexbox
Smooth rotation animation: the block rotates out, swaps to the new shape, then rotates back into place — avoids jarring/instant snapping
Game Over overlay: full-screen dimmed backdrop with a centered white card showing a large "GAME OVER" heading, final score, high score, and a "Play Again" button
Reset button now only appears inside the Game Over overlay, no longer visible during active gameplay

🐛 Bugs Fixed

Rotate/reset buttons losing functionality due to duplicate IDs or missing variable declarations
CSS display: none misplaced, permanently hiding a button even when its parent overlay was shown
Placement logic misaligned for asymmetric shapes (e.g., the T-piece) due to incorrect anchor calculation

📁 Files

index.html — game markup (grid, tray, rotate button, game-over overlay)
style.css — layout, grid styling, shadows, overlay/modal styling, animations
script.js — game logic: board state, shape generation, placement validation, line clearing, scoring, rotation, localStorage persistence
